@startuml Composite-BOM-Problem-Objects
title THE PROBLEM as objects — the wheel exists twice, and 32 spokes are 32 list entries

skinparam objectAttributeIconSize 0

object "bicycle : Assembly" as bicycle {
  BIKE-CITY
  parts = [ saddle ]
  subAssemblies = [ frame, wheel1, wheel2 ]
}

object "frame : Assembly" as frame {
  FRAME-ASM
  parts = [ tubeset, fork, paint ]
}

object "wheel1 : Assembly" as wheel1 {
  WHEEL-ASM
  parts = [ rim, spoke x32, tire, tube ]
  = 35 entries
}

object "wheel2 : Assembly" as wheel2 {
  WHEEL-ASM
  parts = [ rim, spoke x32, tire, tube ]
  = 35 entries
}

object "hub1 : Assembly" as hub1 {
  HUB-ASM
  parts = [ axle, bearing x2 ]
}

object "hub2 : Assembly" as hub2 {
  HUB-ASM
  parts = [ axle, bearing x2 ]
}

bicycle --> frame
bicycle --> wheel1
bicycle --> wheel2
wheel1 --> hub1
wheel2 --> hub2

note right of wheel2
  <b>Two wheel objects, not one.</b>

  There is no way to say "two of these",
  so the wheel had to be BUILT TWICE.
  They are equal in every field and
  identical in no way the code can use.

  Change the spoke count on wheel1 and
  wheel2 does not follow: the product is
  then quietly wrong by one wheel's worth
  of spokes ($397.60 instead of $399.20).
end note

note bottom of bicycle
  <b>85 child-list entries</b> for one
  traversal, and there are three
  traversals in the codebase.

  The Composite version reaches the
  same totals from 14 objects and
  13 line entries — see
  Composite-BOM-Solution-Objects.png.
end note

@enduml
